<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petrobey Mavromichalis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1765">1765</a>–<a href="/years/1848">1848</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Petrobey, Petros Mavromichalis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petros Mavromichalis, known as Petrobey, was the last bey of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mani">Mani</a> peninsula under Ottoman suzerainty. In March 1821 he raised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maniots">Maniots</a> at the start of the Greek War of Independence and led the Messenian Senate at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalamata">Kalamata</a>. He later opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannis-kapodistrias">Ioannis Kapodistrias</a>, whose imprisonment of him led his kinsmen to assassinate the governor in 1831.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petrobey-mavromichalis.jpg" alt="Petrobey Mavromichalis" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Theodoros Vryzakis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%CE%92%CF%81%CF%85%CE%B6%CE%AC%CE%BA%CE%B7%CF%82,_%CE%98%CE%B5%CF%8C%CE%B4%CF%89%CF%81%CE%BF%CF%82_-_%CE%A0%CE%B5%CF%84%CF%81%CF%8C%CE%BC%CF%80%CE%B5%CE%B7%CF%82_%CE%9C%CE%B1%CF%85%CF%81%CE%BF%CE%BC%CE%B9%CF%87%CE%AC%CE%BB%CE%B7%CF%82.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
